<title>USA: U.S. Treasury market in Tokyo closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>U.S. Treasury market in Tokyo closed for holiday.</headline>
<text>
<p>0030 GMT-- *U.S. Treasury market in Tokyo closed on Monday for Martin Luther King Day in United States. *Trading will resume on Tuesday. *Treasuries prices ended flat to slightly higher in shortened session on Friday in New York, with 30-year bond ending up 1/32 at 95-26/32 to yield 6.83 percent.</p>
</text>
